    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 112328\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n328 PM PST Wed Nov 11 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Warm and mild weather will come to an end on Friday as cool,\n  unsettled weather returns to the region with the weather pattern\n  remaining active going into next week. \n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...through next Wednesday.\n\nDry, mild conditions and warmer than normal temperatures will \ncontinue into Friday as ridging persists over the area. The first in \na series of systems will move along the US-Mexico border on Friday. \nIncreased cloud cover on Friday morning and afternoon will be the \nonly noticable impact of this first wave. However, a second trough \nwill follow right on the heels of the first system. This second \ntrough will be stronger, with a more robust plume of moisture \nassociated with it. The Sierra will intercept most of this moisture, \nwith a Winter Storm Watch in effect for elevations above 7,000 feet \nin the Eastern Sierra on Friday and Saturday. Up to a foot of new \nsnow will be possible in the Sierra Crest, with around 5 to 10 \ninches of snow expected between 7,000 feet and 9,500 feet. East of \nthe Sierra, light showers will be possible with the precipitation \nchances will be best in the higher terrain of the southern Great \nBasin and in northwestern Arizona Friday into Saturday. In addition \nto increased precipitation chances, this second system will also \nbring gusty southerly winds to the southwestern Great Basin, Death \nValley, and the western Mojave Desert. A Wind Advisory is in effect \nfor the aforementioned areas starting Friday, continuing into \nSaturday; expect 20 to 30 mph sustained southerly winds with gusts \nto 50 mph in these areas. The second system will clear out of the \narea on Saturday, with a transient shortwave ridge setting up over \nthe area on Sunday, which will provide a brief lull before the next \nsystem swings in early next week. This parade of troughs will \ncontinue through much of the week keeping the weather unsettled and \ncooler than normal.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 00Z Forecast Package...\nLight winds persist and follow typical, daily patterns. Chances for \n10+ knots are 10% or less throughout the TAF period. Light and \nvariable northerly winds to continue through sunset, then expect a \nwind shift to the SW after 03z with speeds remaining under 6 kt. \nSimilar wind pattern expected tomorrow as light NE winds develop \nduring the afternoon. VFR conditions under clear skies.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 00Z Forecast Package...Light and diurnal winds \nanticipated across much of the region through the TAF period, with a \nfew exceptions. At KIFP, local terrain effects will induce northerly \nwinds of 10-15 knots and gusts around 20-25 knots through sunset, \nthen remain elevated overnight. Stronger southerly winds also \ndevelop at KBIH tomorrow afternoon after 20z with sustained winds \naround 15 kt and gusts approaching 30 kt at times. VFR conditions \npersist under clear skies.\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Stessman\nAVIATION...Moore\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
